🔍 Keyword Segmentation: Brand vs Non-Brand Terms
⚙️ Categories Explanation:
•	Brand Keywords: 
o	Include brand names and their misspellings. 
o	Example: "Apple iPhone," "Samsung Galaxy."
•	Non-Brand/Unbranded/GENERIC Keywords: 
o	All other keywords excluding brand mentions. 
o	Includes competitor names as well. 
o	Examples: "smartphone," "laptop deals."
________________________________________
📈 Performance Differences Between Categories:
Category	Characteristics	Typical ACoS
Brand Terms	Higher intent; user knows desired product/brand already	Lower (more efficient)
Non-Brand Terms	User still deciding; broader search	Moderate
Competitor Terms	Effort to change consumer's mind about preferred brand	Highest (least efficient)
________________________________________
🔄 Important Considerations:
•	Volume Availability: 
o	Brand terms have lower available volume than non-brand terms. 
o	Organic traffic may be cannibalized if over-reliant on branded PPC campaigns.
•	Market Share Growth Strategy: 
o	Competitor-focused keyword targeting helps acquire new customers but comes with higher costs due to lower conversion rates.
